      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Tibbie grew in the early 1900s as a rural hub for farming and timber, centered around its post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tibbie_alabama",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Tibbie Store, a one‑story gable‑front wood‑frame building from the 1920s, was the town’s post office until 1998.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tibbie_alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1999 the Tibbie Store was added to the Alabama Register of Landmarks and Heritage for its commercial and architectural value.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/tibbie_alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Tibbie experiences hot summers with highs near 91°F, cool winters dropping to 36°F, and about 60 inches of rain each year, making it prone to Gulf storms.",
